<title>SWEDEN: Sweden's PM says state finance problems are over.</title>
<headline>Sweden's PM says state finance problems are over.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's Prime Minister Goran Persson said on Tuesday that the state's financial problems were over.</p>
<p>&quot;We will never again slip down into a state financial bog,&quot; Persson told a seminar of his ruling Social Democrats.</p>
<p>&quot;When we now have taken a grip on public finances we will keep a grip.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Barbara Taltavull, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1019</p>
